    "spouse_ur": "تسنیم فاطمہ",
    "notes": "Elders recall he was a newborn, or not yet born, when Syed Hussain Ali Rizvi passed away around 1950. Confirmed as the \"Ghulam Raza\" shown in the shajra as a child of Syed Hussain Ali Rizvi. The shajra's death year of 2013 is incorrect — he passed away on 1 January 2015 in Dubai. His wife's full name is Tasneem Fatima, of Naqvi descent; the shajra's \"Tasneem Naqvi\" was a shortened form.\n\nResidence timeline (from a document in his own handwriting, titled \"Life Movement,\" No. 24743):\n1947-48 (1 year): India, Murshidabad\n1948-56 (8 years): Dacca\n1956-61 (5 years): Nilphamari\n1961-66 (5 years): Rajshahi\n1966-74 (8 years): Dacca\n1974-77 (3 years): Karachi\n1977-97 (20 years): Dubai and so on\nSummary totals: Bangladesh 26 years, Dubai 20 years, Pakistan 3 years, India 1 year (total 50 years). Separately noted \"Upheaval in life\": 1966-1971 and 1982-1983 (10 years) -- the 1966-1971 span covers the Bangladesh Liberation War period while he was based in Dacca, a plausible connection though not stated explicitly in the document.\n\nNote: this document's first entry (1947-48, Murshidabad, 1 year) suggests a birth year of 1947, which is in tension with the elders' recollection (recorded above) that he was a newborn or not yet born when Syed Hussain Ali Rizvi passed away c. 1950. Confirmed as the youngest of Syed Hussain Ali Rizvi's children, ruling out a mix-up with a sibling's timeline -- the tension between the two birth-year accounts remains genuinely unresolved.",
    "notes_ur": "بزرگوں کو یاد ہے کہ تقریباً ۱۹۵۰ء میں سید حسین علی رضوی کی وفات کے وقت یہ نومولود تھے",
